class UserDAO {
    private $db;
    private $cache;

    public function __construct($db, $cache) {
        $this->db = $db;
        $this->cache = $cache;
    }

    public function updatePassword($userId, $newPassword, $oldPassword) {
        // Validate password strength
        if (!$this->isStrongPassword($newPassword)) {
            throw new Exception("Password must be at least 12 characters long and include letters, numbers, and symbols.");
        }

        // Check current password
        if (!password_verify($oldPassword, $this->getPasswordHash($userId))) {
            throw new Exception("Incorrect old password.");
        }

        // Update password in database
        $hashedPassword = password_hash($newPassword, PASSWORD_DEFAULT);
        $sql = "UPDATE users SET password = ? WHERE id = ?";
        $stmt = $this->db->prepare($sql);
        $stmt->execute([$hashedPassword, $userId]);

        // Clear user session and cache
        $_SESSION['user'] = null;
        $this->cache->delete("user:{$userId}");

        // Log the password update
        $this->logActivity("Password updated for user ID {$userId}");

        return true;
    }

    private function isStrongPassword($password) {
        return preg_match('/^(?=.*[a-z])(?=.*[A-Z])(?=.*\d)(?=.*[@$!%*?&])[A-Za-z\d@$!%*?&]{12,}$/', $password);
    }

    private function getPasswordHash($userId) {
        $key = "user:{$userId}:password";
        if (!$hash = $this->cache->get($key)) {
            $sql = "SELECT password FROM users WHERE id = ?";
            $stmt = $this->db->prepare($sql);
            $stmt->execute([$userId]);
            $result = $stmt->fetch(PDO::FETCH_ASSOC);
            $hash = $result['password'];
            $this->cache->set($key, $hash, 3600); // Cache for 1 hour
        }
        return $hash;
    }

    private function logActivity($message) {
        $logFile = 'activity.log';
        if (filesize($logFile) < 1048576) { // 1MB limit
            file_put_contents($logFile, date('Y-m-d H:i:s') . " - {$message}\n", FILE_APPEND);
        }
    }
}

// Usage example:
$db = new PDO('mysql:host=localhost;dbname=mydb', 'user', 'password');
$cache = new Memcached();
$cache->addServer('localhost', 11211);

$userDAO = new UserDAO($db, $cache);
try {
    $userId = 1;
    $newPassword = "NewSecureP@ssw0rd";
    $oldPassword = "OldPassword123";
    if ($userDAO->updatePassword($userId, $newPassword, $oldPassword)) {
        echo "Password updated successfully.";
    }
} catch (Exception $e) {
    echo "Error: " . $e->getMessage();
}
```

This code provides a basic structure for updating a user's password in a database using a DAO class. It includes validation for password strength, checks the current password, updates the password in the database, clears the user session and cache, logs the activity, and uses caching to improve performance. The usage example demonstrates how to use the `UserDAO` class to update a user's password.']

