The pipeline supports adding new tasks dynamically using the `addTask` method. When a task is added, it is placed into a thread-safe queue, and one of the available worker threads will pick it up and execute it.

This implementation ensures basic thread safety through the use of mutexes and condition variables. However, additional features such as metadata tag management, priority queuing, dynamic resource allocation, caching, and network resilience need to be implemented based on the specific requirements and constraints of the system.']

