The script uses the `subprocess` module to execute the `kubectl` command for applying the Kubernetes manifest and enabling horizontal pod autoscaling. If any of these commands fail, an exception is raised with a descriptive error message.

The script also includes a function `deploy_service` that encapsulates the entire deployment process, generating the manifest, updating environment variables (if provided), applying the configuration to the cluster, and enabling horizontal pod autoscaling.

In the main block, you can specify the service name, image tag, and any environment variables you want to update. Then, call the `deploy_service` function with these parameters to automate the deployment and scaling of your microservices architecture using Kubernetes."]

